index 00000000..52f56ac3
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/authentication.md
@@ -0,0 +1,67 @@
+# Authentication and captcha compatibility
+
+## Confirmed in this repository
+
+The password flow uses `OAuthHttpUrlChainCall`. Previously `need_captcha`
+unconditionally read both `captcha_sid` and `captcha_img` using `getString`.
+An answer containing only a web `redirect_uri` therefore failed before showing
+a challenge. `VKErrorUtils` made the same assumption for API error 14.
+
+`BaseAuthPresenter.b(AuthAnswer)` maps the server's `error_type=too_much_tries`
+to the localized attempt-limit message. This message does not establish that a
+local counter or an expired client secret caused the rejection. The original
+response is needed to distinguish these cases.
+
+## Changes
+
+- Copy optional captcha fields without requiring an image.
+- Recognize both OAuth `need_captcha` and nested API error 14 during login.
+- Display a returned HTTPS challenge on VK domains in a non-exported WebView
+  Activity. The `AndroidBridge.VKCaptchaGetResult` callback accepts the user's
+  completion token. Closing, load failure, interruption and a five-minute timeout
+  terminate the wait without a successful result.
+- Retry the same OAuth/API chain with `success_token`. Image captchas continue
+  to use `captcha_sid` and `captcha_key`. Answers are isolated by request chain,
+  and stale answers are removed when switching challenge types.
+- Handle `X-Challenge: required` / `X-Challenge-Url` before parsing an OAuth
+  response, then retry the original request once with `X-Challenge-Solution`.
+  This does not loop on a persistent challenge or retry an attempt-limit error.
+
+No client IDs or secrets were replaced. No account credentials were used during
+development. A plain server rejection without a challenge remains a rejection;
+this patch does not restore a revoked password grant or implement a new VK ID
+authorization flow or device attestation.
+
+## Verification and remaining device checks
+
+The standalone regression suite is documented in [tests/auth](../tests/auth/README.md).
+The 54 regression checks passed, and Apktool assembled the modified smali and
+manifest/resources successfully. Full Gradle compilation was attempted with JDK
+17 and Android SDK 32, but project configuration stopped with `NDK is not installed`.
+Smali syntax and manifest/resources can also be checked with:
+
+```sh
+java -jar scripts/apktool.jar b smali --use-aapt2 -p scripts/framework -o /tmp/lite-smali-check.apk
+```
+
+That command alone is **not a complete installable mod build**: the Java changes
+must also be compiled and exported through the normal `buildVTLDev` pipeline.
+
+On a device, verify image captcha, web captcha, cancellation/back, rotation,
+network failure, two successive challenges and successful token delivery. Test
+both login and a normal API request. The native sensor bridge reads only the
+requested accelerometer, gyroscope and rotation-vector sensors while the captcha
+Activity is resumed, and unregisters on pause/close. Hardware sensor behavior and
+any domain outside the explicit VK allowlist need device verification.
+No real login or interactive challenge was available in this environment, so a
+successful sign-in, and resolution of `too_much_tries`, are not verified.
+
+## Protocol references
+
+- [VK Captcha Android result contract](https://cloud.vk.ru/docs/en/security/captcha/concepts/reference-sdk/reference-sdk-android)
+- [VK ID SDK error-14 retry](https://github.com/VKCOM/vkid-android-sdk/blob/master/sdk/core/network/src/main/kotlin/com/vk/id/network/http/captcha/Error14HandlingInterceptor.kt)
+- [VK ID SDK header challenge retry](https://github.com/VKCOM/vkid-android-sdk/blob/master/sdk/core/network/src/main/kotlin/com/vk/id/network/http/captcha/HitmanChallengeHandlingInterceptor.kt)
+- Native bridge callback names were checked against VK's published
+  `com.vk.id.captcha:vkid-captcha:0.0.16` artifact. The SDK is not added as a runtime
+  dependency because this application merges Java dex files into a decompiled
+  APK and contains an older, renamed Kotlin runtime.
